{"id": "sevt_01CgGjVcobpiUSpCcdpqBGH2", "content": [{"text": "Confirmed. The per-row `order_items` query appears in the log starting at **14:06** (none before), coinciding exactly with the deploy, and scales up as traffic/cart sizes grow \u2014 driving the p99 ramp.\n\n## Findings\n\n- **p99 onset is 14:06, not 14:30.** Latency ramps from ~75ms to ~410ms between 14:06\u201314:28, then compounds to 4\u20135s after 14:29 as load/cart sizes grow. The 14:30 figure is just when it crossed the pager threshold.\n- **Deploy `371dfe2` (checkout, 14:06:20, alice)** lines up precisely with the ramp. The diff replaces a single batched query (`OrderItem.objects.filter(order_id__in=ids)`) with a **per-row query inside the loop** \u2014 a textbook N+1.\n- **Log confirms:** per-row `SELECT * FROM order_items WHERE order_id = ?` queries first appear at 14:06 and grow steadily thereafter.\n- **`db46df5` (disable catalog cache, 14:18) is a red herring** \u2014 it was rolled back at 14:23, but p99 kept climbing well past that, so it isn't the driver.\n\nFix: revert/forward-fix `371dfe2` back to the batched `order_id__in` query.\n\n> **Root cause:** `371dfe2` \u2014 \"readability\" refactor of the order summary builder reintroduced an N+1 by issuing one `order_items` query per order row instead of a single batched `IN` query.", "type": "text"}], "processed_at": "2026-10-14T05:48:44.857171Z", "type": "agent.message"}
